    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d258-a1">

                <pb facs="0375" n="375" sameAs="frus:frus1861/pg375"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">“<hi rendition="#small-caps">United
                            States Consulate</hi>,<lb/>“<placeName><hi rendition="#italic">Port of
                                Paramaribo</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-09-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 4, 1861</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>“<hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor (but with chagrin) to
                    inform you that the rebel steamer Sumter arrived at this port on the 19th of
                    August, and left on the 31st, having been allowed to coal and refit. I used my
                    best endeavors to prevent it without avail.</p>
                <p>“I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>“HENRY SAWYER.”</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Immediately on the receipt of it I addressed the following note to the
                        minister of foreign affairs.</p>

                    <postscript>
                        <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington</hi>.</p>
                    </postscript>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
